{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, thanks for reaching out. I can see your laptop (BL-LT-0107). It has plenty of free disk space, but it hasn't checked in with IT for about 12 days, which often means it has been closed or left asleep rather than fully restarted. Please save your work and do a full restart (Start > Power > Restart, not just closing the lid), then reply with a few details so we can pinpoint the problem: what exactly happens (for example freezing, slow apps, a crash or blue screen, a error message, or a printing problem), which app or task it happens in, when it started, and whether it began after a Windows update or a new program was installed. If it still happens after the restart, we'll take the next step from there.",
  "internal_note": "Sender Sofia Rossi (user_id 7, Marketing, active, not VIP, no failed logins, not blocked). Only device BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11 Pro): currently offline, last check-in 2026-09-29 (warning: no check-in for 12 days), disk 140 GB free of 256 GB (54.7%), so disk space is not the cause. Ticket is vague ('the thing again'), so the symptom is unknown. Likely the laptop has not been restarted in a long time (KB-019 quick check 2). Asked user for symptom details, restart status, and whether it started after an update or install (KB-019 / KB-028). No actions queued. Escalate to Tier 2 under KB-019 only if the problem persists after restart, updates, and cleanup, or if blue screens or repeated crashes occur. Mailbox at 27.9% of quota, no issue noted. Triage confidence was low; priority P3 is reasonable.",
